## Fixable gap 1 — the generator lands outside the repo's only Python lint lane

`make lint` / `make format-check` are `$(UV_RUN) ruff check` / `ruff format --check`, and `UV_RUN` is `uv --directory skills/sr-search --no-config run --no-sync`, so ruff's cwd is the engine dir. CI's `Lint` and `Format check` steps likewise run under `defaults.run.working-directory: skills/sr-search`. Root `pyproject.toml` has no `[tool.ruff]`, there is no pre-commit config, and the only existing repo-root script is POSIX shell (`scripts/localdev.sh`, wired via `SCRIPTS :=` in the Makefile).

Consequence: `scripts/gen_warehouse_schema.py` would be the first Python file in the repo that no lint or format gate ever sees, and the plan does not decide that. Fix, using the precedent already in the Makefile's `reuse` target (root-cwd invocation of an engine-env tool):

```make
lint: sync
	$(UV_RUN) ruff check
	$(UV) run --project $(ENGINE) --no-sync $(UV_NO_CFG) ruff check $(SCRIPTS)
```

(and the parallel `ruff format` / `ruff format --check` lines). Step 4 already edits the `Makefile`, so this is additive to work in flight, not a new unit. The alternative — placing the generator under `skills/sr-search/` where bare `ruff check` already covers it — also satisfies the stdlib/no-venv constraint (the file would still be run as `python3 skills/sr-search/…`), but breaks the plan's clean "repo tooling lives in `scripts/`" read and makes the Make target uglier. Recommend keeping `scripts/` and extending the lint lane. Either way, the plan must say which.

## Fixable gap 2 — generated body must be link-free (dual-path constraint)

The same bytes are served from two path contexts: `skills/sr-query/references/warehouse-schema.md` (agent-relative) and `docs/advanced/warehouse-schema.md` (site-relative symlink). Any relative markdown link is therefore wrong in at least one context. This is why every existing cookbook recipe body contains **zero** markdown links — the constraint is real and already honored, but only implicitly.

Step 1's output template ("title, logical-relationships note, mermaid fence, short index note") does not state it. `properdocs.yaml` sets `strict: true` with `validation.unrecognized_links: warn` and `anchors: warn`, so a bad relative link fails the docs job; but a link that resolves from `docs/` and is wrong from the skill path fails silently for the agent audience, which no gate catches. Fix: state in step 1 that the generated body carries no relative links (absolute `https://github.com/…` URLs only, if any are wanted at all), and put the human cross-links in the human-owned pages that step 7 already edits.

